    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "For a positive integer $N$, we denote by $p(N)$ the product of the digits of $N$ when written in decimal form. For example, $p(23)=2\\times3=6$. What is the value of the sum $p(10)+p(11)+p(12)+\\dots+p(99)+p(100)$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2025"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "4500"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "5005"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5050"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "None of (A)-(D)"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor the sum",
        "body": "$p(100)=0$. For two-digit numbers $\\overline{ab}$, $p=a\\cdot b$, so\n$$\\sum_{a=1}^{9}\\sum_{b=0}^{9} ab = (1+2+\\dots+9)(0+1+\\dots+9) = 45\\cdot45 = 2025.$$\n\n**Answer: (A) 2025**"
      }
    ],
