    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The figure shows a square of side 2 divided into four triangles. The three grey triangles have the same area. What is the area of the white triangle?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2021-g1112/q18.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac85$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$3\\sqrt5-5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$6-2\\sqrt5$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Set up the equal areas",
        "body": "The white triangle has one vertex at the top left corner $A$ of the square, one at a point $E$ on the right side and one at a point $F$ on the bottom side. Let $E$ be at distance $x$ below the top right corner and $F$ at distance $y$ from the bottom right corner.\n\nGrey areas: top triangle $\\frac12\\cdot2\\cdot x = x$; left triangle $\\frac12\\cdot2\\cdot(2-y) = 2-y$; bottom right triangle $\\frac12(2-x)y$.\n\nFrom $x = 2-y$ we get $y = 2-x$, and then $\\frac12(2-x)^2 = x$, i.e. $x^2-6x+4=0$, so $x = 3-\\sqrt5$ (the other root is larger than 2).\n\nWhite area $= 4 - 3x = 4-9+3\\sqrt5 = 3\\sqrt5-5$.\n\n**Answer: (D)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
