      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "rabbit"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "We do not have enough information to know for sure"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Where is the rabbit?",
        "body": "The rabbit lives in only one house. If it lived in neither A nor C, the first and third statements would both be true — too many. So the rabbit is in A or in C, and exactly one of these two statements is true.\n\nTherefore the other three statements are false: B has the cat, D has the dog, and A has the **mouse**. Then the rabbit is in C, so the first statement is the true one, and indeed exactly one statement is correct.\n\n**Answer: (C) mouse**"
      }
    ],
